ty prediction from unrelaxed structures. It contains relaxed structures of the MP training set, initial+relaxed structures of the WBM test set, plus several checkpoints for models trained on this data specifically for this benchmark.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">For a description of each file, see https://matbench-discovery.materialsproject.org/data#--direct-download.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The full MPtrj training set containing 1.3M structures along with their energies, forces, stresses and magmons is available at <a href=\"https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/23713842\" target=\"_blank\">https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/23713842.</a></p>", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 39, "status": "public", "size": 17241042260, "created_date": "2026-10-19T08:56:28Z", "modified_date": "2026-10-19T08:56:28Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 1, "name": "CC BY 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"}, "tags": ["materials discovery", "inorganic crystal stability", "machine learning", "interatomic potential", "Bayesian optimization", "high-throughput search", "convex hull"], "keywords": ["materials discovery", "inorganic crystal stability", "machine learning", "interatomic potential", "Bayesian optimization", "high-throughput search", "convex hull"], "categories": [{"id": 25144, "title": "Inorganic materials (incl. nanomaterials)", "parent_id": 25141, "path": "/25066/25141/25144", "source_id": "340301", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 25162, "title": "Structure and dynamics of materials", "parent_id": 25141, "path": "/25066/25141/25162", "source_id": "340307", "taxonomy_id": 100}, {"id": 25186, "title": "Cheminformatics and quantitative structure-activity relationships", "parent_id": 25174, "path": "/25066/25174/25186", "source_id": "340404", "taxonomy_id": 100}], "references": ["https://janosh.github.io/matbench-discovery", "https://github.com/janos